{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MutableDirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P6VertexQa"},{"text":"> : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols021BidirectionalDirectedA0P"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertices","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/Vertices-swift.associatedtype","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P8VerticesQa"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Index","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa"},{"text":" == ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Keys.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" Each vertex has a key: its index in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Vertices.Index == Int"},{"type":"text","text":"). On a dense"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"representation ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AdjacencyList"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedPseudograph"},{"type":"text","text":") the key is the vertex’s slot, which is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"also its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertexIndex(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":"; on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"StableDirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":" it is the vertex’s position, which never"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"changes while the vertex exists and may leave holes. The underscored members read and write the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"graph by key, with no hashing, so a wrapper hashes a vertex once and then works on keys."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Laws."}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" In addition to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":"’s:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"_key(of: v)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertices.firstIndex(of: v)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"code":"_vertex(atKey:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is its inverse.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For a vertex with key "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"k"},{"type":"text","text":": "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_successors(ofKey: k)"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_predecessors(ofKey: k)"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_outEdges(ofKey: k)"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_inEdges(ofKey: k)"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_outDegree(ofKey: k)"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_inDegree(ofKey: k)"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are the members of the same name without the label, for that vertex."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_successorKeys(ofKey: k)"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_predecessorKeys(ofKey: k)"},{"type":"text","text":" are the far ends’ keys, in the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"same order; "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_sourceKey(ofEdgeAt:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_targetKey(ofEdgeAt:)"},{"type":"text","text":" are the endpoints’ keys."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_insertVertex(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" appends a vertex, which must not already be one, and returns its key:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices.endIndex"},{"type":"text","text":" before the call. Keys of other vertices do not change."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_insertEdge(fromKey:toKey:)"},{"text":" inserts the edge and returns its position. On a simple graph","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AdjacencyList"},{"text":"), an edge already present is not inserted again and its position is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"returned. Inserting an edge changes no key.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_removeVertex(atKey: k)"},{"type":"text","text":" removes the vertex and every edge at it. If the representation fills"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the hole by moving another vertex in (a swap-remove), it returns that vertex’s old key, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the vertex’s key is now "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"k"},{"type":"text","text":"; otherwise it returns "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":" and no other key changes."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"_removeEdge(at:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" removes the edge at a live position and returns it, trapping on any other","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"position. Removing an edge changes no key.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"remove(v)"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_removeVertex(atKey: _key(of: v)!)"},{"type":"text","text":", returning the removed instance."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Key density.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" A wrapper may keep one table entry per 1024 keys, from the smallest live key"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices.endIndex"},{"type":"text","text":", plus O(1) per live vertex: the memory of the representation’s own page"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"table. On a dense representation the keys are "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0..<vertexCount"},{"type":"text","text":". On "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"StableDirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":" the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"span can exceed the vertex count: removals leave holes, and a decoded graph may start at any"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"position (its decoder bounds the span at "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"16 × vertexCount + 64"},{"type":"text","text":" pages). Keys before the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"smallest live key cost nothing."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Key rows."}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"_successorKeys(ofKey:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"_predecessorKeys(ofKey:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" return the stored rows","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"typed as ","type":"text"},{"code":"SuccessorIndices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"PredecessorIndices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", whose elements here are keys. On a dense","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"representation keys and indices coincide. On ","type":"text"},{"code":"StableDirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" the elements are positions,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"which are vertex indices only while the graph has no holes; ","type":"text"},{"code":"successorIndices(ofIndex:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"then unavailable, but the key rows are not.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Not requirements."}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"insert(edge:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" differs in its return type: ","type":"text"},{"code":"AdjacencyList","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"simple, returns ","type":"text"},{"code":"(inserted:memberAfterInsert:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", the multigraphs return the new position, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a wrapper that rejects edges returns an optional. So generic code inserts an edge by key, with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"_insertEdge(fromKey:toKey:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The hooks are underscored because they are for wrappers inside the library: callers use the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"representations’ own ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"insert"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"remove"},{"text":" members, which take vertices.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"role":"symbol","title":"MutableDirectedGraph","modules":[{"name":"GraphProtocols"}],"fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MutableDirectedGraph"}],"externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols015MutableDirectedA0P","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MutableDirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"}],"symbolKind":"protocol","remoteSource":{"fileName":"MutableDirectedGraph.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph.swift#L50"},"roleHeading":"Protocol"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/mutabledirectedgraph"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Initializers","anchor":"Initializers","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/init()"]},{"title":"Instance Methods","anchor":"Instance-Methods","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/insert(_:)","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/remove(_:)","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/remove(edge:)","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/removeAll(keepingCapacity:)","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/removeAllEdges(keepingCapacity:)","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/reserveCapacity(vertexCount:edgeCount:)"]}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A bidirectional directed graph that generic code can mutate: Boost’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MutableGraph"},{"type":"text","text":" concept"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"add_vertex"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"add_edge"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"remove_edge"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"remove_vertex"},{"text":"), for a directed representation. It exists so that a wrapper which adds a rule, such as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedAcyclicGraph"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"can own any of the mutable representations as its base and still run at the base’s speed.","type":"text"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols"]]},"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Inherits From","type":"inheritsFrom","kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph"]}],"references":{"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/DirectedGraph/Vertices-swift.associatedtype":{"abstract":[],"required":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/Vertices-swift.associatedtype","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"associatedtype","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertices","kind":"identifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl","text":"Collection","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"type":"topic","title":"Vertices","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/directedgraph\/vertices-swift.associatedtype"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/MutableDirectedGraph/init()":{"required":true,"fragments":[{"text":"init","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"()","kind":"text"}],"title":"init()","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/init()","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/mutabledirectedgraph\/init()","abstract":[{"text":"The empty graph.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/DirectedGraph":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph","title":"DirectedGraph","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A directed graph: a finite set of vertices and a finite collection of directed edges between"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"them."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"DirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/directedgraph","type":"topic","kind":"symbol"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/MutableDirectedGraph/reserveCapacity(vertexCount:edgeCount:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/mutabledirectedgraph\/reservecapacity(vertexcount:edgecount:)","required":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/reserveCapacity(vertexCount:edgeCount:)","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"reserveCapacity","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"vertexCount","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"edgeCount"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"type":"topic","title":"reserveCapacity(vertexCount:edgeCount:)","abstract":[{"text":"Reserves space for at least ","type":"text"},{"code":"vertexCount","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" vertices and ","type":"text"},{"code":"edgeCount","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" edges.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/DirectedGraph/Vertex":{"abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/Vertex","fragments":[{"text":"associatedtype","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"identifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SH","text":"Hashable","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"title":"Vertex","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/directedgraph\/vertex","role":"symbol","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","required":true},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/BidirectionalDirectedGraph":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A directed graph that also answers in-neighborhoods: Boost’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BidirectionalGraph"},{"type":"text","text":". Kept apart"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedGraph"},{"text":" because in-adjacency usually costs extra storage, and many algorithms only","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"go forward.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/bidirectionaldirectedgraph","title":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph","role":"symbol","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/MutableDirectedGraph/remove(edge:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph\/remove(edge:)","title":"remove(edge:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Removes one copy of "},{"code":"edge","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (the newest, on a representation with parallel edges). Never"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"inserts or removes a vertex."}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"remove","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"edge","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DirectedEdge","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols12DirectedEdgeV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{